<title>ABU DHABI: Gulf Air Airbus aborts takeoff as tyre comes loose.</title>
<headline>Gulf Air Airbus aborts takeoff as tyre comes loose.</headline>
<dateline>ABU DHABI 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Gulf Air aircraft aborted takeoff from Abu Dhabi airport on Monday after a front tyre came loose sending it sliding on its belly, an airline source said.</p>
<p>The source said some of the crew and the 107 passengers on board the Airbus A-320 en route to Cairo via Bahrain were slightly hurt. &quot;They were taken to hospitals in Abu Dhabi for checkups. Some are in shock,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>The incident occurred when the plane taxied prior to takeoff.</p>
<p>He did not have more details, but said the airline would soon issue a statement from its headquarters in Bahrain.</p>
<p>An airport official said Abu Dhabi airport would be closed until 0930 GMT because of the incident.</p>
</text>
